.TH SETUP-ONLINE.SH 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
setup-online.sh \- set up the shell for one DAQ environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B source setup-online.sh
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR \fIpartition\fR]
[\fB\-e\fR \fIenvironment\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B setup-online.sh
prepares the current shell to run \fBots\fR for one environment of one
partition. It:
.IP 1. 4
obtains Kerberos credentials and exports \fBKRB5_PRINCIPAL\fR by
sourcing
.BR get_krb_principal.sh (1);
.IP 2. 4
configures the git/GitHub environment from that principal by sourcing
.BR set_git_env.sh (1),
after which the shell can reach GitHub;
.IP 3. 4
looks the environment's test release directory and setup command out of
the operations YAML;
.IP 4. 4
changes into that directory and sources the setup command.
.PP
.B This script must be sourced, not executed.
It changes the working directory and defines the ots environment in the
calling shell, neither of which survives a subprocess. The login
aliases installed by
.BR install-login.sh (1)
define \fBsetup_online\fR and \fBsetup\-online\fR as
\fBsource $HOME/bin/setup-online.sh\fR for this reason.
.PP
With no \fB\-e\fR the partition's first active environment is used, and
the choice is printed, so a single-environment partition needs no
arguments.
.PP
A missing test release directory is reported along with the
.BR create-environment.sh (1)
command that would create it.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then config file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Operations YAML to read. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_CONFIG\fR.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-partition " " \fINAME\fR
Partition to set up. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_PARTITION\fR. Default:
\fIpartition_0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-environment " " \fINAME\fR
Environment to set up. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_ENVIRONMENT\fR.
Default: the partition's first active environment.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the credential, cd and source steps that would be taken, and
change nothing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and return.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Trace execution with \fBset \-x\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SETUP_ONLINE_SH_OPTS
Extra options, prepended to the command line.
.SH NOTES
The script unsets all of its own variables before returning, so the ots
environment is the only thing it leaves behind in the caller's shell.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 if the configuration or the test release
directory could not be resolved, and 2 for an unrecognised option.
Because the script is sourced, this is the return status of the
\fBsource\fR command rather than a process exit status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up the tracker environment:
.PP
.RS
.nf
source setup-online.sh -z partition_0 -e tracker
.fi
.RE
.PP
Or, with the login aliases installed:
.PP
.RS
.nf
setup_online -e trigger
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-daq.sh (1),
.BR create-environment.sh (1),
.BR get_krb_principal.sh (1),
.BR set_git_env.sh (1),
.BR daq-read-config (1)
